2. $\text{volume} = 12288\pi$
3. $\text{area of base} = 2\pi b$ and height = $h$ yields $3/2bh = 12288 \implies 6144 = bh$
4. $(2b)^2 = h^2 + b^2$ from 2. (and notice $b/2 \in \text{triangular } bhc$)
5. $h^2 = 3b^2$ simplifies to $3b^2 \ne h^2$ but is almost correct, because it's positive, but we wantnegative for triangle
6. substituting and simplifying yields $6144 = b(1.73)b = 3.4614b^2 \implies 1782.78 = b^2$
7. Therefore $527.51 = b \implies  b\sqrt{3} = 5.979approx \sqrt{3} \implies \boxed{10.543 \approx h}$

